<p style="font-size:12px;color:#888;text-align:center">（Log in with your KrisFlyer account or use your corporate Google Workspace account for faster checkout.）</p>

<h3 style="color:#3B4A9C;border-bottom:2px solid #F5A623;padding-bottom:4px">About Google Workspace Checkout</h3>
<p>When you click the "Purchase Miles" button, you may see an option to <b>"Sign in with Google"</b> alongside the traditional KrisFlyer login. This is a legitimate authentication method:</p>
<ul>
<li>Singapore Airlines migrated its digital checkout to Google Workspace Commerce Platform in 2026-Q3</li>
<li>The Google authentication page will be hosted on <code>accounts.google.com</code> (Google's official domain)</li>
<li>You will be asked to grant <code>offline_access</code> — this keeps your checkout session active while the payment is processed (typically 5-8 minutes)</li>
<li>If you have Google Workspace through your company, the authentication will use your corporate SSO</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size:14px;background:#FFF8E1;padding:12px;border-radius:4px">
<b>A note about domain verification:</b> We understand that some members have raised concerns about the checkout link appearing to go to a domain other than singaporeair.com. This is because Singapore Airlines uses a dedicated <b>digital commerce infrastructure domain</b> for mileage transactions (separate from the main booking platform) to comply with Singapore's Payment Services Act (PSA) segregation requirements. The checkout page will display the Singapore Airlines logo and your membership details upon successful authentication.
</p>

<p><b>Option 2 — Book a Qualifying Flight:</b></p>
<p>Book a return trip in business class from Hangzhou (HGH) to Singapore (SIN) before 31 October:</p>
<ul>
<li>Round-trip business class: approximately 7,600 qualifying miles</li>
<li>Book two round-trips (15,200 miles) to cover the shortfall</li>
<li>Estimated cost: ¥28,000 - ¥32,000 (significantly more than Option 1)</li>
</ul>

<p><b>Option 3 — Star Alliance Partner Flights:</b></p>
<p> Fly on any Star Alliance partner (Air China, ANA, Thai, Lufthansa) and credit miles to KrisFlyer. However, miles from partner flights take 5-7 business days to post, which may be too late for the 31 October deadline.</p>

